 "identification_note": "Observational: who participates where is self-selected; associations of activity with return are not effects of making a community more active.",
 "extrapolation_limits": "GH Archive public GitHub events, 2024-10-07..10 UTC (Monday to Thursday): participation by non-bot, non-owner accounts in public issue and pull-request discussions. The simulator may use this model for the probability that an individual who has just taken part in a community or project discussion takes part again in the same community within a day, as a function of the community's recent activity and maintainer activity and of the individual's own activity. It may NOT infer: (1) participation in non-software communities, private spaces or other platforms; (2) horizons beyond 24 h or retention over weeks (the window has four days); (3) causal effects of maintainer responses or community size (observational: active repositories attract active developers); (4) the content or quality of contributions (only event types are seen); 'first participation' is first within the window, so earlier history before 2024-10-07 is unknown (left-censored).",
